From b3118c9d953a0976ea81ca892bce2cf9191c36de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:36:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] Staking: a routine session re-read no longer breaks
 approve-then-stake; plainer stake form

Owner test 2026-10-27: the approval was mined, then the pane showed 'wallet, network or sign-in changed' and never offered Confirm stake. The auth client re-reads the session about once a minute with a new object (same address and expiry); the wallet controller's guard compared objects and EconomyPane reset its flow on every new object. Both now use the sign-in's value (sameSession / address+expiry); a new sign-in or another wallet still stops the flow (tests changed to a new expiry; a same-value copy now keeps authority, and reverting the guard fails that test).

Stake form: '1 share = 100,000 EMBEO' in the label, the total with thousands separators, and the review button says what it does ('Next: check allowance') with a line explaining the approve and confirm steps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
